  "summary": "Following Washington's new Driver Privacy Act (SB 6002), Stanwood is reactivating its 14 Flock cameras in compliance with the law, while Spokane County Sheriff's Office is deactivating its ALPR system, citing legal risk. Pierce County previously made the same decision.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Standwood's Flock Camera System will be reactivated later this month following Washington Governor Bob Ferguson's signing of the Driver Privacy Act",
      "paragraph_idx": 5
    },
    {
      "quote": "This new state law imposes significant restrictions on ALPR systems, some of which were ill-considered, leading us to make this difficult decision",
      "paragraph_idx": 14
    }
